{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ie/reviews/id155078609"}, "name":{"label":"Ryaners87"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-11-19T04:03:54-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"2025.11"}, "id":{"label":"13416244828"}, "title":{"label":"Great podcast app for iOS"}, "content":{"label":"I’ve been using Overcast for years & can’t imagine going back to the Apple podcast player. Chapters, podcast notes & embedded images are handled smoothly, Smart Speed is great for accelerating slow or less “professional” speakers without sounding unnatural, I love that when I skip around or pause & unpause I can have Overcast resume from a break in speech vs. halfway through a word. And I especially love that when I accidentally delete the app, like I did 5 mins ago, Overcast will simply sync with its servers on reinstallation so I don’t lose all my podcasts, history & play markers (I may have panicked just a little ngl). There are plenty of granular options to customise the app to how you prefer to listen & navigate through podcasts, many of which can be set per-podcast, & you can tell the developer is a podcast fan too. Now that streaming is back, I have 0 quibbles with the app. The lack of creepy tracking & algos plus commitment to the open spirit of podcasting (vs. Spotify for e.g.) is also a big plus. I listen to MANY hours of podcasts every week & am always happy to recommend Overcast to other folks with iPhones. Keep up the great work! \nPS: Orange rules 🧡", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ie/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ie/reviews/id568716385"}, "name":{"label":"__random_ios_user__"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-11-08T04:32:28-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"2025.11"}, "id":{"label":"13371850204"}, "title":{"label":"Love it….but…."}, "content":{"label":"I love the minimalism. \n\nI love that the default settings work perfectly out of the box.\n\nI love the no-nonsense UX where 90% of what I want is on a single page. \n\n I love the way voice boost and silence trim “just work” and work so well, that you forget they’re active. \n\n As for the down-sides of Overcast…. \n\n It falls down in the ability to discover new podcasts. The “recommended for you” section is abysmal and US-centric. It’s difficult if not impossible to find new podcasts. \n\n In a similar vein, the search feature is very limited and seems constrained to podcast hosts. So you want to find other podcasts that your favourite guest has appeared in?Good luck with that.\n\n I know there’s a re-write of the app in the works. I hope it adds new features and doesn’t just mimic the current functionality. I’m a premium subscriber for the last 6 years but I’m finding it increasingly difficult to justify staying with this app.\n\n [Updated Sept 2024] The new rewritten version had a fairly messy initial rollout, with numerous bugs and missing features. However, over the last few releases, it has re-established its precious stability and new features are being added again. Still waiting for an improved podcast discovery feature.\n\nUpdate Nov 2025:\nThe rewrite has been done and at this stage, Overcast is back to the stability and usability of the past. But I’ve moved on to another app that has the features I’m looking for.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ie/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
